title: "Bruising in GP consultation",
setting: "GP surgery",
stem: "A 34-year-old woman, Mrs Evans, attends a routine consultation for a medication review. While checking her blood pressure, you notice several distinct, finger-shaped bruises on her upper arms. When asked about them, she becomes highly anxious, avoids eye contact, and says she fell down the stairs. You suspect domestic abuse. As you probe gently, she begins to cry and begs you not to say anything to anyone because her husband is waiting in the reception area and has access to all her medical records.",
