setting: "GP surgery",
stem: "A GP, Dr Lawson, receives a visit from a regular patient, 79-year-old Arthur, who has mild cognitive decline and lives alone. Arthur is accompanied by his nephew, who acts as his informal carer. During the consultation, Arthur mentions that he cannot afford his new prescription medication because his bank account is empty. The nephew quickly interrupts, laughing it off and stating that Arthur simply forgets where he spends his pension money. Dr Lawson notices that Arthur looks visibly anxious, shrinks back into his chair, and looks at his nephew for permission before answering any further medical questions.",
