id: "sjt-19-gifts-bequest-in-patient-will",
title: "A Bequest in a Deceased Patient's Will",
setting: "GP surgery",
stem: "Dr. Harriet, a long-serving GP partner, receives a letter from a local solicitor's firm. The letter informs her that a wealthy patient whom she looked after for over fifteen years has recently passed away. In her will, the patient left a personal bequest of £10,000 specifically to Dr. Harriet as a personal thank you for her 'outstanding devotion and medical care over the years.' The patient had no immediate family, but has living nieces and nephews who are currently contesting other aspects of the estate's distribution.",
