title: "Critical Omission During ICU Step-Down Handover",
setting: "ward",
stem: "You are an FY2 doctor working on a general medical ward. A patient is stepped down from the Intensive Care Unit (ICU) to your ward midday. The ICU verbal handover is brief, focusing on the patient's respiratory recovery. However, upon reviewing the electronic chart hours later, you notice that a critical infusion of an antiarrhythmic drug was stopped during the transfer, and no oral alternative was prescribed or handed over. The patient is currently asymptomatic but has a history of unstable atrial fibrillation.",
