title: "Disagreement with community physiotherapist on urgent referral",
setting: "GP surgery",
stem: "Dr. Hobbes, a GP, receives a call from a community physiotherapist who is evaluating a patient with lower back pain. The physiotherapist suspects early signs of cauda equina syndrome and requests that Dr. Hobbes arrange an immediate emergency hospital admission. Dr. Hobbes feels that the physiotherapist is overreacting based on a brief assessment and prefers to see the patient himself in a routine slot later that week.",
