stem: "You are a Foundation Year 1 (FY1) doctor working on a busy medical ward. A senior staff nurse, Nurse Reynolds, asks you to review a patient whose National Early Warning Score (NEWS2) has triggered a clinical alert. After examining the patient, you conclude that their condition is stable and no acute intervention is required. When you explain your clinical reasoning to Nurse Reynolds, she becomes visibly angry and snaps at you in front of other staff members, stating that you are being reckless and ignoring clear signs of deterioration. She demands that you order a chest X-ray and immediate blood tests.",
