setting: "ward",
stem: "You are an FY1 doctor working on an acute medical ward. An 82-year-old patient admitted from a nursing home with a suspected urinary tract infection is noted to have a National Early Warning Score (NEWS2) of 6, including a temperature of 38.9°C and mild confusion. The senior staff nurse advises you that she believes the patient is septic and needs immediate broad-spectrum antibiotics. You have not yet had a chance to examine the patient yourself, and you are currently completing discharge summaries for three patients who are waiting to leave the hospital.",
