explanation: "This is a very appropriate response because the locum's poor technique poses an immediate risk of severe infection and procedural complications (such as pneumothorax) to an unstable patient. Patient safety requires direct, immediate intervention to halt unsafe practice, regardless of the colleague's seniority. Escalating to intensive care ensures expert help arrives quickly."
