id: "sjt-03-consent-advance-decision-refusal-treatment",
title: "Valid Advance Decision to Refuse Treatment",
setting: "emergency department",
stem: "A 60-year-old man with terminal lung cancer is brought to the Emergency Department with severe pneumonia and acute respiratory failure. He is drowsy and unable to communicate effectively. His daughter arrives and hands you a legally signed and witnessed 'Advance Decision to Refuse Treatment' (ADRT) document created six months ago. The document explicitly states that the patient refuses mechanical ventilation and intubation if his cancer becomes terminal. The attending registrar wants to intubate anyway.",
